## 🛠️ Phase 2: CI/CD Stabilization & Hybrid Brain

I addressed the failing GitHub Actions caused by broken dependencies and the shift to Local-First AI.

### Key Fixes

1. **Hybrid LLM Client**: Upgraded [llm_client.ts](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/src/swarm/llm_client.ts) to support both **Ollama (local)** and **Cloud APIs (OpenAI/Anthropic)**.
   - Automatically falls back to Cloud in GitHub Actions environments.
   - Preserves privacy and zero-cost local inference on the USER's machine.
2. **Singularity Restoration**: Switched [intelligence_pulse.ts](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/swarm/intelligence_pulse.ts) from legacy code to the modern [SingularityEngine](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/swarm/core/singularity_engine.ts#34-355).
3. **Loop Cleanup**: Removed stale references to [RevenueHunter.ts](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/swarm/agents/RevenueHunter.ts) in [swarm/core/loop.ts](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/swarm/core/loop.ts).
4. **CI/CD Stabilization**:
   - Standardized GitHub Workflows on **Node.js 22** to support modern dependencies.
   - Fixed path redundancy in [quantum_evolution.yml](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/.github/workflows/quantum_evolution.yml) to resolve `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND`.

